    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are parallel horizontal circles measuring angular distance North or South of the Equator (0°).",
        "Longitudes are vertical semi-circles running from pole to pole, measuring angular distance East or West of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Earth completes a 360° rotation in 24 hours, equivalent to 15° per hour or 1° every 4 minutes.",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is calculated from the 82.5° E longitude passing through Mirzapur, Uttar Pradesh.",
        "Crossing the International Date Line (180° Longitude) from West to East gains a day, while East to West loses a day."
      ],
      "id": "gn3l7ip"
    },
